{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02950",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.76,
      "end_seconds": 6.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "hello, take a seat, I'll be with you in a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.17,
      "end_seconds": 8.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Hi there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.12,
      "end_seconds": 11.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "start wherever you like, I'm listening"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.37,
      "end_seconds": 20.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Yeah, it's a new headache at the temple. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.39,
      "end_seconds": 23.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Alright, did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.91,
      "end_seconds": 39.18,
      "duration_seconds": 13.27,
      "text": "Sorry, uh, what was I saying, it's been going on for about a month. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.31,
      "end_seconds": 45.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.41,
      "end_seconds": 62.69,
      "duration_seconds": 16.28,
      "text": "right, maybe a three out of ten on a bad day it's worse with touching it's once or twice a day. Blurred vision in one eye was there, but it's gone away on its own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.84,
      "end_seconds": 80.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "Let me check a a few things. Any shoulder stiffness, fever or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.6,
      "end_seconds": 85.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "mm, nope, nothing like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.81,
      "end_seconds": 91.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "On the the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.83,
      "end_seconds": 95.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "oh, no, that's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.33,
      "end_seconds": 101.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.46,
      "end_seconds": 106.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Warfarin. I take it in the evening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.04,
      "end_seconds": 109.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.7,
      "end_seconds": 115.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "3 milligrams, I think that's what's on the the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.16,
      "end_seconds": 120.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Alright, how long has that that been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.62,
      "end_seconds": 136.74,
      "duration_seconds": 14.12,
      "text": "Nearly five years now. I take clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day. Work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.41,
      "end_seconds": 140.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "when did you start it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.68,
      "end_seconds": 143.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.39,
      "end_seconds": 148.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.69,
      "end_seconds": 155.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "I've had an irregular heartbeat, yes. I've had heart disease, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.1,
      "end_seconds": 164.71,
      "duration_seconds": 8.61,
      "text": "Okay, go on. Yes, heart disease is known to us, good to have that clear. Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.86,
      "end_seconds": 180.31,
      "duration_seconds": 14.45,
      "text": "I had two stents put in my heart three years ago. My family kept telling me to get it checked. My neighbour said I should get it looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.85,
      "end_seconds": 194.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.23,
      "end_seconds": 202.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.76,
      "end_seconds": 206.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.27,
      "end_seconds": 211.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 223.8,
      "end_seconds": 233.57,
      "duration_seconds": 9.77,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pressure 108 over 80, heart rate 71, temp 36.6 degrees, SpO2 98 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.91,
      "end_seconds": 235.61,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.09,
      "end_seconds": 241.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "right, let's have a proper look at you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.61,
      "end_seconds": 245.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.82,
      "end_seconds": 248.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "breathe out slowly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.32,
      "end_seconds": 261.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "The temporal artery is hard, tender and has no pulse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.82,
      "end_seconds": 280.69,
      "duration_seconds": 13.87,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. Putting it all together, I'm honestly not certain yet. It could be possible giant cell arteritis threatening sight, or it might be a migraine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.74,
      "end_seconds": 283.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.17,
      "end_seconds": 305.53,
      "duration_seconds": 20.36,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's possible giant cell arteritis threatening sight, and we'll watch how it goes. I think the rheumatology team should see you too. Do get help quickly if you lose vision. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.45,
      "end_seconds": 309.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "yeah, alright, thanks, take care"
    }
  ]
}